\ A redefinition inside a word body that declares a matching stack effect must not warn about
\ dropping the declaration. Both definitions land in the body's own transient frame, so the
\ second is a same-scope redefinition of the first. The declaration travels attached to the
\ quotation literal, so a compiled body must deliver it to the redefinition checks exactly as the
\ interpreter does. This file runs under both the interpreter and eager suites against the same
\ goldens.

use "testing" ;

"word-body redefinition keeps its declared effect" test-section

make-stored: ( -- s ) [
  val: ( -- s ) [ "A" ] ;
  val: ( -- s ) [ "B" ] ;
  val
] ;

make-stored "B" "redefinition with matching declared effect runs silently" assert=
